1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,183
The emperor gives a thumbs down.

2
00:00:04,333 --> 00:00:06,750
Except... nobody knows that.

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,150
Gladiators: the thumbs down myth.

4
00:00:09,300 --> 00:00:13,183
Roman writers say the crowd turned their thumbs.

5
00:00:13,333 --> 00:00:16,050
Turned which way? They never said.

6
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:19,150
It might have been up. Or sideways.

7
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:22,717
Some think a hidden thumb meant mercy.

8
00:00:22,867 --> 00:00:25,617
So where did thumbs down come from?

9
00:00:25,767 --> 00:00:28,850
A painting. 1872.

10
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,783
A French artist painted the crowd, thumbs down.

11
00:00:32,933 --> 00:00:35,017
It was a huge hit.

12
00:00:35,167 --> 00:00:37,750
Then the movies borrowed it.

13
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:41,017
Also, most fights didn't end in death.

14
00:00:41,167 --> 00:00:44,450
Gladiators were expensive to train.

15
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,183
Losing one was like wrecking a sports car.

16
00:00:48,333 --> 00:00:51,517
Many walked out alive, to fight again.

17
00:00:51,667 --> 00:00:54,550
Some even became celebrities.

18
00:00:54,700 --> 00:00:57,650
Which way the thumb went: unknown.

19
00:00:57,800 --> 00:01:01,417
Roman sources saying "thumbs down": zero.

20
00:01:01,567 --> 00:01:05,350
Anyway, here's the emperor. Thumbs down.
